# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.09738) is a technique that mitigates measurement errors and is useful for estimating Pauli observable expectation values. It relies on measurement twirling (randomly injecting an `X` gate before the measurement and flipping the measured result), which diagonalizes the readout-error transfer matrix and makes it easy to invert. A rescaling term is learned from the diagonal noise channel by measuring twirled calibration circuits that were initialized in the zero state.\n"
msgstr "[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.09738) adalah teknik yang memitigasi error pengukuran dan berguna untuk mengestimasi expectation value observable Pauli. Teknik ini bergantung pada measurement twirling (menyuntikkan gate `X` secara acak sebelum pengukuran dan membalik hasil yang terukur), yang mendiagonalkan matriks transfer error readout dan membuatnya mudah diinvers. Suku penskalaan ulang dipelajari dari kanal noise diagonal dengan mengukur circuit kalibrasi twirled yang diinisialisasi dalam keadaan nol.\n"

