# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the entangling layers' noise {#learn-the-entangling-layers-noise}"
msgstr "Pelajari noise layer entangling {#learn-the-entangling-layers-noise}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit. If you assume a Markovian noise model, the depth of the circuit is assumed to not affect the noise channel of a given entangling layer.  Therefore, only the noise model of each unique layer of entangling gates should be learned. The circuit used in this guide can be split into two unique layers. Designing circuits to have a minimal set of unique entangling layers is important if you want to learn a noise model, since the unique layers must be learned independently. If you have too many unique layers in your circuit, noise learning can become infeasible due to the sampling cost of learning many layers.\n"
msgstr "PEC diawali dengan mempelajari model noise twirled dari setiap layer gate entangling di dalam circuit. Jika kamu mengasumsikan model noise Markovian, kedalaman circuit diasumsikan tidak memengaruhi kanal noise dari suatu layer entangling.  Karena itu, hanya model noise dari setiap layer gate entangling yang unik yang perlu dipelajari. Circuit yang dipakai di panduan ini dapat dibagi menjadi dua layer unik. Merancang circuit dengan himpunan minimal layer entangling unik itu penting jika kamu ingin mempelajari model noise, karena layer-layer unik harus dipelajari secara independen. Jika circuit kamu punya terlalu banyak layer unik, pembelajaran noise bisa menjadi tidak layak karena biaya sampling untuk mempelajari banyak layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`qiskit-noise-learning` is used to learn the noise. The learner repeats each layer _`fragment_depths`_ times in its learning circuits, twirls each circuit _`num_randomizations`_ times, and fits the decay of the measured fidelities to a Pauli-Lindblad model. These parameters can effect the accuracy of the learned model. The more accurate the learned noise model is, the more accurate the noise cancellation will be.\n"
"The following code draws the learned noise model with the two layers merged into one map. Each qubit is a pie of its weight-1 X, Y and Z rates summed over the two layers, and each edge shows the learned weight-2 rates. For example, a rate of ``3e-4`` means that error occurs on roughly three of every 10,000 uses of the layer.\n"
msgstr ""
"`qiskit-noise-learning` dipakai untuk mempelajari noise. Learner mengulang setiap layer sebanyak _`fragment_depths`_ kali di dalam circuit pembelajarannya, men-twirl setiap circuit sebanyak _`num_randomizations`_ kali, lalu mencocokkan peluruhan fidelity hasil pengukuran ke model Pauli-Lindblad. Parameter-parameter ini dapat memengaruhi akurasi model yang dipelajari. Makin akurat model noise yang dipelajari, makin akurat pula pembatalan noisenya.\n"
"Kode berikut menggambar model noise yang dipelajari dengan kedua layer digabung menjadi satu peta. Setiap qubit berupa diagram pie dari laju X, Y, dan Z berbobot-1 yang dijumlahkan pada kedua layer, dan setiap edge menunjukkan laju berbobot-2 yang dipelajari. Misalnya, laju ``3e-4`` berarti error itu terjadi kira-kira tiga dari setiap 10.000 kali pemakaian layer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Readout noise mitigation is done in post-processing by using TREX, as opposed to the **gate** noise model, which is required for the program preparation in order to inject the anti-noise that corresponds to the learned noise model.\n"
"Therefore, the readout noise can be either executed and learned when learning the gates' noise, or when executing the mitigated program. Learning the readout noise alongside the gate noise might be beneficial for learning a self-consistent noise model (see [Disambiguating Pauli noise in quantum computers](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.22629) for example). In cases where the gate noise and the readout noise are separated in the noise model, it is recommended that you learn the readout noise when executing the mitigated program to avoid drift in the noise between the when it was learned and executed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mitigasi noise readout dilakukan pada post-processing dengan memakai TREX, berbeda dengan model noise **gate**, yang diperlukan untuk persiapan program agar dapat menyuntikkan anti-noise yang sesuai dengan model noise yang dipelajari.\n"
"Karena itu, noise readout dapat dijalankan dan dipelajari saat mempelajari noise gate, atau saat menjalankan program yang dimitigasi. Mempelajari noise readout bersamaan dengan noise gate mungkin bermanfaat untuk mempelajari model noise yang konsisten satu sama lain (lihat misalnya [Disambiguating Pauli noise in quantum computers](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.22629)). Dalam kasus ketika noise gate dan noise readout dipisahkan dalam model noise, disarankan agar kamu mempelajari noise readout saat menjalankan program yang dimitigasi untuk menghindari drift noise antara saat noise dipelajari dan saat dijalankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this guide, the readout noise is learned while executing the mitigated program by using TREX calibration circuit.\n"
msgstr "Dalam panduan ini, noise readout dipelajari saat menjalankan program yang dimitigasi dengan memakai circuit kalibrasi TREX.\n"

